entry.summary:
This work focuses on the nonhomogeneous nonlocal double phase problem \begin{align*}
  L_au(x)=f(x,u,D_s^p u, D_{a,t}^q u) \text{ in } Ω, \end{align*} where $Ω\subset\mathbb{R}^N$ is a bounded domain with Lipschitz boundary, $0<s,t<1<p\leq q<\infty$ with $tq\leq sp$ and the operator $L_a$ is defined as \begin{align*}
  L_a u(x)&=2\operatorname{P.V.}\int_{\mathbb{R}^N}|u(x)-u(y)|^{p-2}(u(x)-u(y))K_{s,p}(x,y)
  &\ \ \ +2\operatorname{P.V.}\int_{\mathbb{R}^N}a(x,y)|u(x)-u(y)|^{q-2}(u(x)-u(y))K_{t,q}(x,y)dy. \end{align*} We establish the equivalence between weak and viscosity solutions under boundedness and continuity assumptions. In addition, the local boundedness of weak solutions in some special cases on $f$ is also obtained using the notion of De Giorgi classes.

For a Banach lattice $X$, its lattice Schäffer constant is defined by: \begin{gather*}
  λ^+(X)=\inf\{\max\{\|x+y\|,\|x-y\|\}\,\colon\,\|x\|=\|y\|=1,x,y\geq{\bf0}\}. \end{gather*}
  In this paper, we investigate this constant, as well as the companion parameter \begin{gather*}
  β(X)=\inf\{\|x\vee y\|\,\colon\,\mbox{$\|x\|=\|y\|=1$, $x,y\geq{\bf0}$ and $x\wedge y={\bf0}$}\}. \end{gather*} Our main results fall into two groups. (1) We link the behavior of the parameters $λ^+$ and $β$ to the global properties of the lattice $X$. For instance, we prove that (i) if $λ^+(X)>1$, then the Banach lattice $X$ is a KB-space, and moreover, it satisfies a lower $q$-estimate for some $q\in(1,\infty)$; (ii) $λ^+(X)=1$ if and only if $X$ contains lattice-almost isometric copies of $\ell_\infty^2$; and (iii) that $λ^+(X)=2$ if and only if $X$ is an abstract $L$-space. (2) We establish inequalities relating $λ^+(X)$ to the characteristics of monotonicity, $\varepsilon_{0,m}(X)$ and $\tilde\varepsilon_{0,m}(X)$. Along the way, we compute $λ^+(X)$ and $β(X)$ for various Banach lattices $X$.
